cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MeetMind in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "MeetMind: open-source AI meeting notes for Windows and macOS"
abstract: >-
  MeetMind is an open-source desktop app for Windows and macOS that records system audio and
  microphone, transcribes meetings with AssemblyAI, Google Cloud Speech-to-Text,
  Sarvam AI or Groq, generates meeting minutes with Google Gemini, Groq or Anthropic Claude, and syncs them to
  Notion. On Windows it detects Google Meet, Zoom and Teams calls and offers to record from a floating
  overlay; an optional Chrome extension adds a record button inside Meet and Zoom tabs.
authors:
  - given-names: Aslah
    alias: aslahtp
repository-code: "https://github.com/aslahtp/meetmind"
url: "https://aslahtp.github.io/meetmind/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - AI meeting notes
  - meeting transcription
  - meeting minutes
  - speech-to-text
  - speaker diarization
  - Google Meet
  - Zoom
  - Notion
  - Gemini
  - Groq
  - Claude
  - Electron
